            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am not entirely sure what is going on here.\r\n\r\n'mini.files' indeed is quite forceful when it comes to its view. It [updates window border highlight on every view change](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e2273ec6186a7af206cc73de10970c0c3867c46d/lua/mini/files.lua#L2153-L2154)  (which includes moving cursor). So it seems not to be about visual feedback on modified buffer, but about which plugin takes control over `FloatBorder` highlight group in 'winhighlight'. If it is the case, I am afraid there is indeed not much 'mini.files' can do because it seems reasonable for it to have control over borders of its windows. \r\n\r\nAlso I *think* [overriding whole 'winhighlight'](https://github.com/A-Lamia/spotlight.nvim/blob/a42fa49be359fffc5a94dc0b9cbea5c6d651a69a/lua/spotlight/core.lua#L43) will not play well with plugins setting other parts of 'winhighlight'.",
